      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're absolutely right; the failure to find objective meaning can indeed feel like an exhausting battle against an indifferent universe. However, many philosophers argue that if value is subjective, the \"work\" you feel it takes to create your own is actually the most meaningful thing you can do. By claiming your own purpose, you transform the universe from a cold void into a space where your life directly matters, making the struggle less of a losing battle and more of an act of defiance.",
      "source": "target",
